# Everything outside the course tree that changes on a WSL-looking machine whose only
# missing piece is systemd in wsl.conf.
#
#   /etc/wsl.conf   the change -- but see below, this fixture's run.sh arranges the starting
#                   state at boot, so the path appears whichever way the installer went and
#                   it is the CONTENT report that distinguishes the four states
#   /work           the read-only mount this harness adds, not the installer
#   the bare dirs   mtimes
#
# Notably ABSENT and worth noticing: no /etc/passwd, no /etc/shadow, no /etc/subuid. Unlike
# the subuid fixture, nothing here goes near the shadow suite -- setup_wslconf is two file
# writes and touches nothing else, which is the claim.
A /etc/wsl.conf
A /work
C /etc
C /home
C /home/student
C /tmp
